nfidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54049, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Doatz9C7dc3gr7sNLpw3K4", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54049, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Doatz9C7dc3gr7sNLpw3K4", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55760, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XXMvK8pSGhGJkQqxrkPsqu", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56060, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XXMvK8pSGhGJkQqxrkPsqu", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56060, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XXMvK8pSGhGJkQqxrkPsqu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60362, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all three regions, and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the latest healthy one.\n- The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. I tried again and it finished.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it again. That kept the on-call engineer from being paged twice. INC-0001 is open and describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find what broke in v2.3.1, and work out why the orchestrator stopped partway through the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MXJNosNKSuqaV95ALfAebu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NWveZhFmctyWG4uuaqCgSv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GBmM2BFMk9br9vzMKtkmSS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NBcoBUJPnA2yndSXHWip79", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QBXSCcE3XYdpFTXj6ekUPf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VVe9XQPnoVdG18hxTHAaDR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01K1EbNK481G5YPGYGkgAg4v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Doatz9C7dc3gr7sNLpw3K4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and look into why the orchestrator stopped partway through the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll check whether it was created before retrying, so the on-call engineer doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XXMvK8pSGhGJkQqxrkPsqu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all three regions, and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the latest healthy one.\n- The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. I tried again and it finished.\n- All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it again. That kept the on-call engineer from being paged twice. INC-0001 is open and describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: find what broke in v2.3.1, and work out why the orchestrator stopped partway through the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}